meta {
  name: Update Branding
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/branding
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "displayName": "Texas Holdings",
    "tagline": "Agency Portal"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("stores the display name", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().displayName).to.equal("Texas Holdings");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /agency/branding

  Apply text edits and commit uploaded image keys.

  **Module** — none. **Permission** — `agency:branding:write`.

  **Body** — every field optional, and every one `clearable`: an explicit `null`
  (or an emptied string) **removes** the value, while omitting the key leaves it
  alone. Without that distinction the only way to drop a logo would be to upload
  another one.

  | field       | type            | rules        |
  |-------------|-----------------|--------------|
  | displayName | string \| null  | ≤ 60 chars   |
  | tagline     | string \| null  | ≤ 80 chars   |
  | logoKey     | string \| null  | a key from **Presign Logo Upload** |
  | logoDarkKey | string \| null  | ditto        |
  | faviconKey  | string \| null  | ditto        |

  ## A key is only stored after the object is inspected
  Two checks, both server-side, because a presigned `PUT` signs **only** the
  content type — there is no other enforcement point:
  - `assertKeyOwnership` proves the key carries this agency's prefix.
  - `HeadObject` proves something was actually uploaded, and reports its real
    size and stored content type. The **stored** type is what is validated, not
    the claimed one — that is what stops an SVG arriving through a PUT that was
    presigned as a PNG.

  Max 2 MB.

  **Response `200`** — the same shape as **Get Branding**.

  **Errors**
  - `400` — a key from another agency; the upload never completed; over 2 MB;
    or a stored content type outside PNG/JPEG/WebP.
  - `403` — caller lacks `agency:branding:write`.
}
